    "sections": {
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/suredash</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>SureDash &gt; Settings</strong> to configure your dashboard.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='how%20can%20i%20report%20a%20security%20bug%3F'>\nHow can I report a security bug?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>We take plugin security extremely seriously. If you discover a security vulnerability, please report it in a safe and responsible manner.</p>\n<p>You can report the issue through our <a href=\"https://brainstormforce.com/bug-bounty-program/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Bug Bounty Program</a>.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.2.1 &#8211; 31st July 2025</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Improvement: Default Rest Password mail template updated with the new {{password_reset_url}} variable.</li>\n<li>Fix: Removing &#8220;Space Thumbnail Image&#8221; still be visible in the space collection frontend.</li>\n<li>Fix: Opened image Lightbox able to scrolls beneath portal view.</li>\n<li>Fix: &#8220;Login to Contribute&#8221; CTA notice visible for non logged-in users even if post comments are disabled.</li>\n<li>Fix: SureCart Compatibility &#8211; Customer dashboard areas are not rendering.</li>\n<li>Fix: Kadence Compatibility &#8211; Global theme palette vars not loading on the portal frontend.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.2.0 &#8211; 25th July 2025</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New: Introducing &#8220;Copy URL&#8221; functionality for comments, allowing users to easily copy the URL of a specific comment.</li>\n<li>New: Introducing &#8220;Edit&#8221; functionality for comments, allowing users to edit the comment.</li>\n<li>New: Introducing &#8220;Delete&#8221; functionality for comments, allowing users to delete their own comments.</li>\n<li>New: Compatibility of Collection Space with the SureDash premium plugin. (https://suredash.com/docs/create-collection-space/)</li>\n<li>Improvement: The flow of space creation and setting up has been improved with better user experience.</li>\n<li>Improved codebase with best coding practices.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Separated the Space Title &amp; Space Icon fields in the Space creation flow for better user experience.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Duplicated space name for Posts Discussion space type is restricted for avoiding same forum name conflicting issue.</li>\n<li>Fix: Compatibility for Presto Player for their future update to fix paginated posts with media blocks are not rendering properly on the frontend.</li>\n<li>Fix: Comments separator line not appearing properly in continuous comment threads.</li>\n<li>Fix: Duplicated SureDash post falls under the last paginated page of the post list.</li>\n<li>Fix: Google GSI login not working properly in the SureDash Login/Register block.</li>\n<li>Fix: Portal spaces &amp; community content&#8217;s post comments are not appearing under the user profile view.</li>\n<li>Fix: Hidden space creation notification is suppressed.</li>\n<li>Fix: SureDash capability user unable to upload image/video from comment box.</li>\n<li>Fix: Query Monitor shows &#8220;Function _load_textdomain_just_in_time was called incorrectly&#8221; error.</li>\n<li>Tweak: Updated &#8220;Failed to Save&#8221; error message when non portal-manager user tries to save the space settings.</li>\n<li>Tweak: A portal-manager user is deleted from the WordPress user list, then this user is removed from the portal manager list.</li>\n<li>This update addressed a security bug. Props to PatchStack for reporting it responsibly to our team. Please make sure you are using the latest version on your website.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.1.0 &#8211; 08th July 2025</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New: Introducing &#8220;User Roles&#8221; filter for Users table in the admin dashboard to filter users based on their roles.</li>\n<li>New: Introduced &#8220;Override WordPress Registration Setting&#8221; option in the Login/Registration settings to allow registration even if the WordPress registration is disabled.</li>\n<li>New: Introduced new keyboard shortcut (CTRL+S / CMD+S) to save the space editor &amp; space group settings.</li>\n<li>New: Added lost-password &amp; reset-password support for the SureDash Login block.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Added better validation notices for images upload in the frontend post editor if image size exceeds the limit.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Introduced &#8220;Link&#8221; option for Reset Password email template setting to allow users to put a custom links in the email.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Refactored the code for dashboard app icon library for better performance.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Added support for searching posts and pages by their ID in the single space post search.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Improvised the flow of user profile form updating and saving process with better user experience.</li>\n<li>Improvement: Optimized dashboard application performance for better user experience with improved codebase.</li>\n<li>Fix: SureForms form CPT posts getting listed in single space post search results.</li>\n<li>Fix: Kadence compatibility: The scroll to top buttons appear weirdly on the portal frontend.</li>\n<li>Fix: Profile&#8217;s Save button isn&#8217;t working on Safari browser.</li>\n<li>This update addressed a security bug. Props to PatchStack for reporting it responsibly to our team. Please make sure you are using the latest version on your website.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.3 &#8211; 26th June 2025</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Improvement: Added settings notice for Login/Registration page if site&#8217;s User Registration is disabled.</li>\n<li>Fix: Profile photo&#8217;s &#8220;Upload&#8221; button wraps to the next line with word wrap.</li>\n<li>Fix: Like &amp; Share buttons getting hidden if comments disabled for the single space.</li>\n<li>Fix: GIF posting always come aside to the description text.</li>\n<li>Fix: Like &amp; Share buttons getting hidden when comment setting disabled from single space.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "description": "<p>SureDash transforms your WordPress site into a vibrant community hub. Create a unified login and dashboard experience to boost user engagement—all within your WordPress environment. Unlike standalone platforms like Circle, SureDash integrates seamlessly with your existing WordPress setup. Keep full control over your data and customize the experience to fit your brand. <span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"750\" height=\"422\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7syWO6epxnE?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></p>\n<h3>Key Benefits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Seamless Integration:</strong> Enhance your WordPress site with community features.</li>\n<li><strong>Customizable Design:</strong> Tailor the dashboard and features to match your brand’s look and feel.</li>\n<li><strong>Scalable Solution:</strong> Add new spaces as needed.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Free Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Custom login and registration forms</li>\n<li>Visual customizer for dashboard layout</li>\n<li>User profiles</li>\n<li>Activity feeds for updates and engagement</li>\n<li>Discussion forums with threaded replies (only site admin can post, but all members can comment)</li>\n<li>Multiple discussions for focused sub-communities</li>\n<li>Giphy integration for animated GIFs</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>SureDash Premium</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Learning management system course builder</li>\n<li>Enable users to post in discussion feeds</li>\n<li>Private discussion feeds</li>\n<li>Resource library (coming soon)</li>\n<li>Events (coming soon)</li>\n<li>Support from our team</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Perfect For</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Membership sites</li>\n<li>Online courses</li>\n<li>Customer support hubs</li>\n<li>Niche communities</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Links</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Visit <a href=\"https://suredash.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">SureDash</a></li>\n<li>Get <a href=\"https://suredash.com/support\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Support</a></li>\n<li>Check <a href=\"https://zipwp.org/plugins/suredash/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Live Demo</a></li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
